>> title: Sweet and Sour Pork
>> category: Stir-Fries
>> tags: pork, pineapple, chinese, deep-fry, wok
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: sweet and sour pork, sweet & sour pork, gu lo yuk, gu lao rou, 咕嚕肉, 咕噜肉
>> pairs-with: sweet-and-sour-sauce, egg-fried-rice
>> servings: 4
>> time: 50 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the first fry cooks the pork through and the second crisps it, and the two cannot be merged into one
>> washing-up: the wok, a bowl to marinate in, a dish to dredge in, a rack to drain on

>> step: marinate 20 min
Marinate @pork shoulder{1 1/4%lb}(560 g; cut in 1-in cubes) with @Shaoxing wine{1%Tbs}, @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, and @egg{1%large}(beaten) for ~marinate{20%min}.

>> step: dredge dry, shake off the loose
Dredge @&(~1)marinated pork{} in @cornstarch{3/4%cup}(90 g), pressing it on, then shaking off what does not cling.

>> step: fry 350°F 5 min, again at 375°F 2 min
Fry @&(~1)coated pork{} in @peanut oil{4%cups}(950 mL) in two batches at 350°F (175°C) for ~fry{5%min}, rest it on a rack, then return every cube to the oil at 375°F (190°C) for ~fry{2%min}.

>> step: stir-fry 2 min, keep them crunchy
Stir-fry @green bell pepper{1%medium}(cut in 1-in squares), @onion{1/2%medium}(cut in petals), and @pineapple chunks{1%cup}(165 g; drained) in a hot #wok{} for ~stirfry{2%min}, only until the edges take colour.

>> step: pour the sauce in, simmer 1 min
Pour @sweet and sour sauce{1 1/2%cups}(355 mL) over @&(~1)vegetables{} and ~simmer{1%min} until it turns glossy.

>> step: toss to coat, serve at once
Toss @&(~3)fried pork{} through @&(~1)sauce{} off the heat and serve at once — the crust holds for about a minute, which is the whole reason it is fried twice.
